description:
Owner feedback: 'it's not clear what the sidebar does or how to add or rewire components.'

The left sidebar is the palette of 14 pieces. Today:
- Adding is by dragging a palette entry onto a wire (insert) or onto a piece of the same family (swap). Dropping anywhere else does nothing.
- Connecting is by dragging from a piece's small output dot to another piece.
- Rewiring an existing wire has no direct gesture. You connect a new wire into the port, which replaces the old one, or delete the wire.
None of this is signposted.

Work, within the CLAUDE.md rule that the tool contains no lesson text (labels, settings and one-sentence messages only):
- clear affordances: palette header/label, drag handles, hover and press states, drop-target highlighting while dragging (wires and pieces light up as valid targets), visible input/output ports with larger hit targets;
- a direct rewire gesture: drag a wire's end to another port, possibly coordinated with the 'drag everything' bead;
- tap-to-add as an alternative to drag (select a palette entry, then tap a wire);
- short tooltips/titles per palette entry (the piece name and what it connects to, one plain phrase);
- an empty or first-run state that makes the gestures discoverable without tutorial text.
Ask the owner if any guidance text beyond labels is wanted; that would be an exception to the no-lesson-text rule.
